<Concept title="Dodge" section="Mechanics">
  <p><em>Placeholder — not yet specified.</em></p>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <p>Will define the dodge roll: travel distance, duration, cooldown, and the invincibility (i-frame) window, tunable per weapon. The animation clip length scales the move phase, so distance is partly weapon-driven.</p>

  <h2>Reference</h2>
  <p>The in-repo <code>dodge-debug</code> tool (web mock at <code>#/dodge-debug</code>) visualizes the roll and i-frames for tuning — to be ported here as an interactive view.</p>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/player/player.gd</code> (Player) — <code>_start_dodge</code> caches the facing direction and scales the move phase to the active weapon's <code>_esc_f</code> clip length; <code>_handle_dodge</code> drives the roll at <code>DODGE_SPEED</code> for the move fraction (with an edge check so it won't roll off a ledge), then zeroes velocity through the recovery and returns to IDLE.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Status: <strong>implemented (#273)</strong> — <code>take_damage</code> is a no-op while DODGING during the move phase (<code>dodge_timer &lt; dodge_move_end</code>, the first <code>DODGE_MOVE_FRACTION</code> of the clip); the recovery crouch + rise is vulnerable. <code>test_player_states</code> pins both sides of the window.</p>

  <p><a href="/mechanics">← Mechanics</a></p>
</Concept>
